# BOHEMIA ACT ONE ASK -- PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# A02 -- THE ELDER'S ACCIDENT
#
# HIS OWN LINE, from the locked element set:
#   "THE ELDER'S ACCIDENT -- he is ready to show you the truth about Dubai and is
#    killed by something that does not add up before he can; you inherit the
#    locked family box. (The mystery seed. REVEALS NOTHING ABOUT THE
#    AMALGAMATION.)"
#
# *** THAT PARENTHESIS IS A HARD LIMIT AND THIS FILE OBEYS IT. *** Nobody here
# learns anything. The box does not open. Dubai is a word an old man was about to
# say and did not. Writing the reveal would be inventing the single most
# expensive piece of canon in the game inside a side ask.
#
# THE ASK IS A CLAIM: they say it was an accident. A claim is checked by GOING TO
# THE THING, never by a skill roll and never by a highlighted line, because 118 of
# 158 measured deception cues mean nothing and people catch lies 47% of the time.
# So you go and look at where he fell, and what you find is that it does not add
# up -- which is his own words -- and NOT who did it.
#
# WHAT VISIBLY CHANGES: what people say. You either let the accident stand or you
# say out loud that it was not one, and the valley's opinion of your family moves
# either way.
#
# WHAT THIS JOB PAYS, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE SAME THING TWICE: every ending gets
# the box, so the quiet ending is paid in the box (resources) and the two loud
# endings are paid in what people now say about you (clout). One currency per
# ending, one unit each. What you spent to get it is the difference.
#
# draft:true. Every line is an attempt and not one word is approved.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# @STUDY Q003.W8  THE WITNESS WHO KNOWS
#   applied: the one who was actually there carries the truth the people paying for the funeral would rather not hear, and you can side with either.
# @STUDY Q039.W9  PERCEPTION-GATED TRUTH
#   applied: cited as the thing we REFUSE. No build, stat or perception gates whether you see the lie here; the ground does, and the ground is the same for everybody.
# @STUDY Q046.X5  HEIRS INHERIT HATRED
#   applied: the box passes to you and nothing else does, so the inheritance is a question rather than a bonus, which is the named fix for a handoff that feels arbitrary.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_a02_the_elders_accident   The Elder's Accident
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE kin      REQ  block=same
@ROLE witness  OPT  block=same

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The old man died on the slope behind his own house. Everybody is calling it a fall.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG Went and stood where he landed. It does not add up and I cannot tell you why it does not.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Kept it to myself. Took the box he left and put it somewhere nobody looks.
  @DO pay resources 1
  @DO set_flag has_the_box
  @DO learn it_does_not_add_up
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Said it at the burial, in front of everybody. That it was not a fall. Nobody argued and nobody agreed.
  @DO pay clout 1
  @DO set_flag has_the_box
  @DO set_flag said_it_at_the_burial
  @DO learn it_does_not_add_up
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Told the one person who was up there that night that I know they were up there.
  @DO pay clout 1
  @DO set_flag has_the_box
  @DO set_flag named_the_witness
  @DO learn it_does_not_add_up
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Let it be a fall. The box is still in his house and I have not been back for it.

@OBJ 10  "Go and look at where he fell"   target=kin
@OBJ 20  "Decide what it was"             target=kin

# =====================================================================
# THE CLAIM. An accident, stated by somebody who needs it to be one.
# =====================================================================
@TALK claim  speaker=kin  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY He went off the slope behind the house. That is all. He was old and it was dark. #grief
  @SAY I know what people are going to say and I am asking you not to be one of them.
  @SAY He wanted to show you something first. He said that to me twice this month and he never said what.
  @OPT "Show me where."             [gate: none]  -> where
  @OPT "What did he want to show me?" [gate: none]  -> what
  @OPT "Alright. It was a fall."    [gate: none]  -> let
  @OPT (go and look anyway)          [gate: none]  SILENCE -> where
  @NOVERB "Who did this"
@END

# THE HARD LIMIT, IN THE FICTION. He does not know, and nothing in this quest
# can buy the answer, because the answer is canon nobody has ruled.
@TALK what  speaker=kin
  @SAY Dubai. That is the whole of it. He said the word and he said not yet and then he was going to bed. #tired
  @SAY There is a box in his room with a lock on it he never explained either. It is yours now, he wrote that down years ago.
  @OPT "Show me where he fell."     [gate: none]  -> where
  @OPT (say nothing)                [gate: none]  SILENCE -> where
@END

@TALK let  speaker=kin
  @SAY Thank you. #grief
  @OPT (go and look anyway)         [gate: none]  SILENCE -> where
  @OPT (leave it)                   [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
@END

@TALK where  speaker=kin
  @SAY Behind the house, past the wire. Mind the loose ground. #grief
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

# =====================================================================
# THE SLOPE. The ground is the only witness that cannot be lying, and all
# it says is that this is wrong. It does not say who.
# =====================================================================
@TALK slope  speaker=witness  entry=stage>=20
  @SAY You are standing where I was standing. #wary
  @SAY Look at it. He came off there and landed here, and a man who falls does not land that far out. I have carried enough of them to know.
  @SAY That is what I have got. I do not know who and I am not going to guess in front of you.
  @OPT "Then I keep it quiet."      [gate: none]  -> quiet
  @OPT "Then people should hear it." [gate: none]  -> loud
  @OPT "You were up here that night." [gate: none]  TRAP -> you
  @OPT (look at the ground a long time) [gate: none]  SILENCE -> quiet
  @NOVERB "Tell me what was in the box"
@END

@TALK you  speaker=witness
  @SAY I was. I have said so to anybody who asked, which is you. #dread
  @SAY And if you go down there and say my name, that is the end of me on this block whether I did it or not. You know that.
  @OPT (say their name anyway)      [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
  @OPT "I'm not saying your name."  [gate: none]  -> quiet
@END

@TALK quiet  speaker=witness
  @SAY Then take his box and let them bury him as a man who fell. #grief
  @OPT (take the box, say nothing)  [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @OPT "No. They should hear it."   [gate: none]  -> loud
@END

@TALK loud  speaker=witness
  @SAY At the burial, then, with all of them there, and you had better be ready for what comes after. #dread
  @OPT (say it at the burial)       [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT (keep it quiet after all)    [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
@END
